  "articleBody": "Ensuring a senior's home is safe and comfortable is super important, and a systematic approach to repairs can really help. First, check all entryways. Are handrails secure? Are steps even and free of cracks? Make sure exterior lighting is bright enough to prevent trips and falls. Next, move inside to the bathroom and kitchen, which are often high-risk areas. Test all grab bars to ensure they're firmly attached, check for leaky faucets that could cause slippery floors, and make sure appliance cords aren't frayed or obstructing walkways. Consider adding non-slip mats in wet areas. Then, look at the general living spaces. Are carpets securely tacked down? Is there adequate lighting throughout the house, especially in hallways and stairwells? Are smoke detectors and carbon monoxide alarms working and properly placed? Finally, assess the overall structural integrity; look for any signs of water damage, loose floorboards, or wobbly railings. If you spot anything that seems unsafe or beyond a simple fix, don't hesitate to reach out. HH Remodeling LLC can help with those crucial safety repairs, from minor fixes to larger accessibility modifications, ensuring peace of mind for you and your loved ones. Call us at 303-505-0866 for service in the Denver area, including Littleton and Highlands Ranch.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
